  "proof": {
    "original": "For exactly one source, choice equals consumer presence (or 1 for unconditional goals). When active, support time equals source end or initial time t0-1.",
    "forward": "Substitute that time into precedence and all threat checks, and enforce producer presence under the original consumer activation guards. Every old schedule satisfies the new encoding.",
    "reverse": "Extend a new assignment by setting choice to consumer presence and, when active, support time to the unique source time. When inactive, assign any in-domain support time. This satisfies the old encoding.",
    "scope": "Zero-source and multi-source encodings, all instance limits, protection checks, interval locks, time domains and objective remain unchanged. Unique means execution instance, not activity definition.",
    "consequence": "Same projection to execution selection/times, hence same feasible schedules and lexicographic optimum, conditional on original model correctness."
  },
